{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2904","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2904","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2904\",\"parent_revision\":\"38074d9f382c953e24c4f1b64986227e087bcce8\",\"root_revision\":\"802a19cd69939e46905d9ce8b18309ab610f777aa5dec6f7e513beb41fd8c2e1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered while fixing #2900 (PR #2902). Unlike priority/issue and other backward-compatible flat fields, BacklogItem.reference is not kept in sync with metadata.issue by the _sync_metadata model validator. PR #2902 heals this at the GitHub backend's read boundary (_stable_reference() in load_records()), but the underlying design gap remains: any future write path that doesn't route through put_work_item()/load_records() could reintroduce the same class of bug (reference silently empty while metadata.issue holds the real value). A deeper fix would fold reference under the same validator-enforced invariant as the other synced fields \u2014 a larger, more invasive model change than the read-boundary patch in #2902.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor(backlog-mcp): backlogitem.reference not kept in sync with metadata.issue by model validator** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"689e0aab8bb8045628b14aa2018db856d8ef58dde7181b6965b99b0bacb330b8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPToi4g\"}"}